abstract: >-
  A native Rust engine for InSAR time-series analysis of ground deformation
  from Sentinel-1 data (PS-InSAR and Small-Baseline Subset), with a native
  ISCE reader, quality-guided and SNAPHU unwrapping, robust SBAS inversion
  (OLS/WLS/L1-IRLS) with DEM-error estimation, native non-closure phase-bias
  correction, LiCSAR reader, GACOS/ERA5 tropospheric correction, LOS
  decomposition and per-pixel ML features. Numerical parity with MintPy 1.6.3
  on the Fernandina Sentinel-1 stack (series RMSE 0.034 µm, r = 1.000000).
  Consumable as a Rust library, CLI, and Python bindings (insar-rs on PyPI).
keywords:
  - InSAR
  - SAR interferometry
  - ground deformation
  - SBAS
  - persistent scatterers
  - Sentinel-1
  - remote sensing
  - Rust
